# API conventions

- Layers per module in `modules/<name>/`: `*.routes.ts` → `*.service.ts` → `*.repository.ts`. Copy the shape of `modules/tickets/` or `modules/comments/`, never `modules/reports/` (legacy).
- Routes: `validate("query" | "param" | "json", schema)` with a schema from `@support-desk/shared`, call one service function with `c.var.context`, return `c.json(result)` (201 for creates, `c.body(null, 204)` for deletes).
- Services take the `RequestContext` first and call `authorize(context, projectId, action?)` from `auth/policy.ts` before touching project data. Cross-project lists are scoped with `visibleProjectIds(context)`. No membership or role checks anywhere else.
- Every change to a ticket's status, priority, assignee or labels writes an activity event with `recordTicketEvents()` inside the same `inTransaction()` as the change. `describeChanges()` in `modules/tickets/ticket-changes.ts` turns a change into events.
- Time comes from `context.clock.now()`, never `new Date()`. Timestamps are UTC ISO strings; days, weeks and business hours are computed in the project's `timeZone` with `lib/dates.ts`.
- Repositories use the Drizzle query builder and return shared types. List and count share one `matchesFilter()`.
- Errors: throw `ValidationError` (400), `ForbiddenError` (403), `NotFoundError` (404) or `ConflictError` (409) from `http/errors.ts`. Hidden and missing resources use the same 404 message.
- Schema changes: edit `db/schema.ts`, run `npm run db:generate -w @support-desk/api -- --name <change>`, update the seed and `db/seed.test.ts`, commit the migration.
- Relative imports end in `.ts`. No enums, no constructor parameter properties (Node strips types at runtime).
